+config ESP32_GDMA
+	tristate "ESP32-S3 general DMA engine"
+	depends on OF && HAS_IOMEM
+	help
+	  The ESP32-S3's general DMA engine, driven memory-to-memory through
+	  one ioctl. It exists because the engine's descriptor list must live
+	  in internal SRAM (TRM 3.4.1), and on this NOMMU kernel a userspace
+	  mmap of that window does not reach it -- remap_pfn_range() installs
+	  nothing without a page table, so the store is lost and the read
+	  returns the old value. The kernel reaches the same address through
+	  ioremap(), so the descriptor is built here instead.
 
+	  It also releases the engine from reset and enables its clock, which
+	  until now had to be done by hand after every boot.
+
+	  This is the first half of the SPI DMA work: it proves the engine
+	  moves bytes before anything is pointed at a peripheral.
